<title>UK: BRITISH ELECTION DIARY - April 21.</title>
<headline>BRITISH ELECTION DIARY - April 21.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is the election diary for Monday, April 21:</p>
<p>Prime Minister John Major, Education Secretary Gillian Shephard and Conservative Party chairman Brian Mawhinney present daily news briefing at 9.15 a.m. (0815 GMT)</p>
<p>Labour Party Shadow Chancellor Gordon Brown, deputy party leader John Prescott and agriculture spokesman Gavin Strang present daily news briefing at 8.30 a.m. (0730 GMT)</p>
<p>Liberal Democrat leader Paddy Ashdown interviewed on BBC 1's Panorama 8.30 p.m. (1930 GMT)</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +4471 542 7950</p>
